WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.234
-A judge ruled

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.167
that official records
from the Trump White House

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.234
could be turned over
to the congressional committee

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.534
investigating
the January 6th insurrection

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:10.300
and, yet, even as Trump
and his allies

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.133
face various investigations
and accusations of wrongdoing,

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.467
they're still reappearing
on right-wing media networks

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:16.601
to lie about everything

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.100
from the pandemic
to the economy.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.167
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:25.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.667
When Trump left office,
there were lots of people

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:30.067
I would've been happy
to never see or hear from again,

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.267
like overinflated football
Jason Miller

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:34.267
[ Laughter ]
or the zombie who somehow

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.467
retained the ability to talk,
Stephen Miller.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.000
[ Laughter ]
[ As Miller ] Yes,
I did catch the rage virus,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.868
and, yes, I do have
an appetite for brains,

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.334
but that should not distract
from the fact

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:44.267
that Joe Biden is
an illegitimate president!

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.934
[ Laughter ]
But, probably, the person

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.501
I miss the least is
Kellyanne Conway,

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.434
whose shamelessness
truly knew no bounds.

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:51.200
She was, somehow,
the Trump administration's

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.300
most prolific,
and also, worst liar.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.934
She wasn't even smooth about it.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.634
She lied the way your kids lie.

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:58.067
Did you do your homework, Teddy?

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.667
"Not only did I do
all my homework

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:02.167
for the entire school year
and all of everyone else's,

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.567
I also did the laundry."

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:06.133
[ Laughter ]
Okay, yeah.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:07.601
Go do your homework.
"What gave it away?

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:08.701
Was it the laundry?"

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.934
[ Laughter ]
To this day, I still think

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:13.033
the quote that should follow her
for the rest of her career is

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.434
this moment from March of 2020,
where she insisted,

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.133
in the most condescending
way possible,

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.567
that the coronavirus outbreak
was under control.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.467
-It is being contained and --

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:23.501
Do you not think it's
being contained

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:24.634
in this country?
-I'm not a doctor.

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.200
I'm a lawyer.
-But you said

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.467
it's not being contained, so,
are you a doctor or a lawyer

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.033
when you say it's not being
contained? That's false.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.067
-The virus is spreading --
-You just said something
that's not true.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.767
[ Laughter ]
-She always sounds like
she's trying to argue

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:36.334
that her coupon is still valid
at Talbots.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.901
[ Laughter ]
[ As Conway ] It's valid.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:38.968
Do you not think it's valid?

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:40.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.133
You said it was not valid
and I'm just wondering

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.501
where you came up
with that it wasn't valid.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.834
[ Laughter ]
But, hey, credit
where credit is due.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.267
She was right.
It was all contained.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.100
The coronavirus went away,
everything went back to normal,

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.501
I kept doing the show
in a suit and tie

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:52.367
in front of a live studio
audience without interruption,

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.801
and I stopped having
that weird recurring nightmare

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:56.901
where I was trapped in a room
with a sea captain painting

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.968
[ Laughter ]
who loved corny jokes

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.300
and sounded suspiciously
like Will Forte.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.100
-Hey, Seth, what do you call
a painting that isn't real?

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.133
-I don't know.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:09.267
-A pigment of your imagination.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:18.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.801
-I got to figure out a way
to get rid of that guy.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.334
So, a deadly respiratory virus

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.000
was rapidly spreading
across the country

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
and, yet, Kellyanne Conway
confidently told us

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.267
everything was under control,

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.701
like a Park Slope mom
sipping a Chardonnay

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.434
while her kids
set the house on fire.

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.667
[ Laughter ]
"Don't worry.
The fire is contained

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.801
and the fumes help build up
their immune system.

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:36.934
Hold on one second.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.334
Juniper!

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:42.367
What did I say
about adding lighter fluid?!

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.634
Juniper!

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:47.701
Stop squirting
the lighter fluid!

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.767
So help me God, Juniper!"

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:52.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:57.300
Hey, you guys,
I'm going to let you

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.400
behind the curtain a little bit.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.200
Wally, old Cue Card Wally,
backstage --

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.968
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah, no, sure. Why not?

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:10.067
Wally said, "Hey,"
because, you know,

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.434
Wally's ahead of the curve...

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:12.801
[ Laughter ]
...so he's trying to stay

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.634
two steps ahead of it,
so we don't get in any trouble,

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.501
he goes, "Hey, you want me
to hold the cards a little off

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:17.567
when you're yelling at Juniper?"

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:20.868
I was like, "Great idea, Wally."

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.367
So I turn that way.

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:23.701
Wally goes that way.

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:26.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.300
Hey, look, I get it, Wally,

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.501
you went the side
that made more sense.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.634
-Thank you.
That's right.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.400
Besides, you always --
-Anyway, uh,

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.067
we're talking about how
someone else is incompetent!

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:40.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.734
And, yet, despite --
or, more likely, because --

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.400
of the fact that she lied
about everything,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.033
Kellyanne Conway was invited
back on Fox News this week

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:49.667
to lie, yet again, this time,

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.400
about global
supply chain issues.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.033
-You have a Biden administration
pretending they can bring us

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.934
out of a once-in-a-century
pandemic economically

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:59.667
and they can't admit
what inflation is.

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:02.501
Joe Biden telling us all
that we're sort of stupid

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:05.467
and don't understand what
the supply chain crisis is.

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:07.400
I worked at that White House
for four years.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.067
-Well --
-We never even heard
of such a thing.

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.167
There wasn't
a supply chain crisis.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:13.267
-Oh, really?
Because I seem to remember

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.834
a time when a roll
of toilet paper

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:17.300
had a street value just
above cocaine.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:20.734
"Hey, man, you, uh,
looking to score some paper?

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:22.968
I just got some sweet
Alabama Snowflake.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.834
Two plys and you'll fly, baby."

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.868
[ Laughter ]
Now, in fairness,

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:28.467
that disruption
to the supply chain

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.033
was caused, in large part,

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:32.100
by panic-buying in the early
days of the pandemic,

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.567
though, I'm still not sure

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.400
why we all stocked up
on toilet paper,

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.400
like we were about to be
surprise guests on "Hot Ones."

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.534
[ Laughter ]
"Sean Evans is here!

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:41.767
He has 10 different sauces!

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:43.767
We need backup!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.968
I still have PTSD
about toilet paper,

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.767
aka TPSD.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.534
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:51.167
The Sea Captain
sent that one in.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.300
Every time I see some dude
walking down the street

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.033
carrying a six-pack of Charmin,
I scream,

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.334
"If you don't have six bathrooms
or six ass[bleep],

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:00.567
you better turn around right now

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.000
and take that back
to the store!"

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.534
[ Laughter and applause ]
Which is a bummer

00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:06.133
because I'm almost always
with my kids when I yell that

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:07.868
[ Laughter ]
and then,

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:09.334
they have a ton of questions.

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:11.000
"Uh...what's an ass[bleep]?"

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.734
Well, I guess you, if you tell
Mommy this happened again.

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:14.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.601
It's not a threat!
It's a definition!

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:19.067
[ Laughter ]
I mean,

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:21.400
I know the last 20 months
have been kind of a haze,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.000
but did they really
expect us all to forget

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.467
the long lines for food
and the empty store shelves

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:27.667
and the desperate search
for Lysol and Purell?

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:29.334
Do they think we've forgotten
the days

00:05:29.334 --> 00:05:30.467
of watching "Tiger King"

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.067
and trying to make
our own hand sanitizer

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:33.834
out of vodka and grape jelly?

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.634
That's not to say there aren't
supply chain issues now.

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:38.868
There obviously are.

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:41.267
I just ordered a Christmas gift
for my wife

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:42.601
and I got an email back
telling me

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:43.834
I should get it by July.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:44.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.334
That's just great.
Hopefully,

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:47.801
the cashmere sweater
will look good

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:49.300
on my divorce attorney.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.667
Happy Independence Day, Irv.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:56.501
You think my wife's going
to believe me

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:57.868
when I say her gift
didn't arrive

00:05:57.868 --> 00:05:59.400
because there were
supply chain issues,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.400
especially since I've used
that excuse before?

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:06.267
Even worse, I used it in 2011.

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:08.267
[ Laughter ]
It seemed genius, at the time,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.834
but last night, she asked,
"Hey, what was

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:12.267
the supply chain issue
in 2011, again?"

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:14.934
And the best I could come up
with was, "Um,

00:06:14.934 --> 00:06:16.434
uh, uh, the royal wedding?"

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:17.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.267
Yeah, I guess like
William and Kate

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:20.801
bought all the bracelets
that year.

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:24.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.834
And, in some ways, I guess
it shouldn't be a surprise

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:27.200
that there are
supply chain issues.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.267
We're still living through
a once-in-a-century pandemic

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:32.200
that has transformed virtually
every aspect of society,

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.834
not to mention
inflationary pressures

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:35.234
that are,
on top of everything else,

00:06:35.234 --> 00:06:36.434
making life difficult

00:06:36.434 --> 00:06:37.767
for working people
in this country.

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:40.734
Democrats need to deal
with those issues ASAP.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:43.234
Unfortunately, we got
an unhinged Republican Party

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:46.000
that loses its [bleep] if just
a handful of their members vote

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.601
for a bipartisan
infrastructure plan,

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:49.434
and millionaire
corporate Democrats,

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:50.801
like Joe Manchin,
standing in the way

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:52.767
of the agenda President Biden
promised to deliver.

00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:54.968
And it certainly
doesn't help the optics that,

00:06:54.968 --> 00:06:56.367
not only does Manchin have
a yacht

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:57.501
that he calls a houseboat,

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:59.300
he also apparently
has a Maserati,

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.767
as we discovered
from a recent clip

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:03.334
where he was confronted
by climate activists.

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:05.601
I'm sorry, but no politician
should have a Maserati.

00:07:05.601 --> 00:07:07.634
Are you a senator
from West Virginia

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:09.667
or a plastic surgeon
from Palm Beach?

00:07:09.667 --> 00:07:11.133
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:13.767
Joe Biden drives a Stingray
and he only gets away with it

00:07:13.767 --> 00:07:15.133
because he has the vibe

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:17.701
of a kind old grandpa
who's getting back into dating.

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:19.434
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:21.200
[ As Biden ]
I'm going to pick up
Nancy Pellegrino

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.234
down in the nursing home.

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:24.367
Oh...Nancy Pellegrino.

00:07:24.367 --> 00:07:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.734 --> 00:07:27.467
I remember back in '59,

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:28.734
when we were
high school sweethearts.

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:30.834
I took her to a drive-in
to see "Ben-Hur"...

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:32.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.968
...and we slid
into the backseat and, well,

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:36.667
let's just say we went at it
like Roman gladiators.

00:07:36.667 --> 00:07:37.868
"Grandpa!"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:40.434
Cars had a lot more steel
in 'em, in those days,

00:07:40.434 --> 00:07:41.501
and so did I.

00:07:41.501 --> 00:07:42.701
"Grandpa, stop it!"

00:07:42.701 --> 00:07:44.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.934 --> 00:07:47.267
The point is,
the supply chain crisis is

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:49.601
[ Laughter ]
very real,

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:51.801
but let's not act like it
just happened out of nowhere.

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:53.300
And the fact that the people
around Trump

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.067
are such brazen, shameless liars
is all the more reason

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:58.834
why we need to see actual
records of what was going on

00:07:58.834 --> 00:08:00.601
behind the scenes
in that White House,

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:03.400
especially as it relates to the
insurrection on January 6th.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.501
Trump has been trying
to keep those records hidden

00:08:05.501 --> 00:08:07.100
from public view, but a court

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.767
just ruled against him
last night.

00:08:08.767 --> 00:08:10.901
-Former President Trump
has lost the latest round

00:08:10.901 --> 00:08:12.300
in his legal battle to keep

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.200
certain White House
records secret,

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.200
relating to the January 6th
attack on the U.S. Capitol.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.801
-A federal judge has ruled

00:08:18.801 --> 00:08:20.934
the congressional committee
investigating

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:24.033
the January 6th attack
on the U.S. Capitol

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:26.267
can access
former President Trump's

00:08:26.267 --> 00:08:27.601
White House records.

00:08:27.601 --> 00:08:29.367
-In this court filing,
very late at night,

00:08:29.367 --> 00:08:32.067
the National Archives
puts out a list

00:08:32.067 --> 00:08:35.000
of more than 700 pages,
itemized, saying,

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.801
"This is what Donald Trump
wants to keep secret,"

00:08:37.801 --> 00:08:40.701
and they really gave details
that we didn't know.

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:43.400
There are these handwritten
memos, or handwritten notes,

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.868
from Chief of Staff
Mark Meadows,

00:08:44.868 --> 00:08:46.834
specifically about January 6th.

00:08:46.834 --> 00:08:50.667
There are call logs
and switchboard call logs

00:08:50.667 --> 00:08:54.434
about calls to President Trump,
to Vice President Mike Pence,

00:08:54.434 --> 00:08:56.801
leading up to about January 6th.

00:08:56.801 --> 00:08:58.234
These are
very specific things --

00:08:58.234 --> 00:09:00.968
White House visitor logs,
White House call records,

00:09:00.968 --> 00:09:03.334
other memos, the daily schedule.

00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:05.934
-I'm shocked to learn there
even was a daily schedule.

00:09:05.934 --> 00:09:09.300
[ Laughter ]
Remember when we found out,
most days, it said...

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.534
and that was just code for Trump

00:09:10.534 --> 00:09:11.734
not wanting
to leave his bedroom?

00:09:11.734 --> 00:09:14.000
He'd just spend the morning
in his PJs,

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.300
calling in to "Fox &amp; Friends,"
while viewers waited

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.601
for them to blink, to make sure
they were still alive.

00:09:18.601 --> 00:09:20.534
[ Laughter ]
Every once in a while,

00:09:20.534 --> 00:09:21.601
an intern would come out

00:09:21.601 --> 00:09:23.767
and smear their eyeballs
with Vaseline.

00:09:23.767 --> 00:09:26.501
[ Laughter ]
Brian Kilmeade always looked,
during those interviews,

00:09:26.501 --> 00:09:27.767
like he was auditioning
to be one

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:30.167
of those gold statue guys
in Times Square.

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:32.133
[ Laughter ]
He never actually went home.

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:34.267
They'd just turn off the lights
and leave him there overnight.

00:09:34.267 --> 00:09:35.734
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.734 --> 00:09:37.701
Maybe that's why Trump
didn't care about the pandemic.

00:09:37.701 --> 00:09:39.767
He was the first president
to work remotely

00:09:39.767 --> 00:09:41.167
and, even when he did
show up to the office,

00:09:41.167 --> 00:09:43.901
I'd be shocked if there
were ever actually records

00:09:43.901 --> 00:09:45.868
or official documents
in that White House.

00:09:45.868 --> 00:09:48.367
You think anyone ever took notes
in a meeting with Trump?

00:09:48.367 --> 00:09:50.467
When they finally subpoena
those notepads,

00:09:50.467 --> 00:09:52.267
they're just going to be filled
with random doodles

00:09:52.267 --> 00:09:53.968
and inscrutable comments,
like...

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.734
And there's no way Trump himself
ever wrote anything down.

00:09:58.734 --> 00:10:00.634
He never even wrote any
of his own books.

00:10:00.634 --> 00:10:03.100
They were ghostwritten, which
I'm sure Trump took literally.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:05.067
[ As Trump ] I didn't write it.
A ghost did and I was

00:10:05.067 --> 00:10:07.701
[ Laughter ]
pretty disappointed
when I met the ghost.

00:10:07.701 --> 00:10:09.133
They said, "Donald,
we're getting you a ghostwriter

00:10:09.133 --> 00:10:10.367
and I was hoping for a Slimer

00:10:10.367 --> 00:10:11.901
or, even better,
a Patrick Swayze.

00:10:11.901 --> 00:10:13.033
[ Laughter ]

00:10:13.033 --> 00:10:14.100
That's the kind of atmosphere

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:15.434
the Trump inner circle fostered

00:10:15.434 --> 00:10:16.534
and, now, it's taken hold

00:10:16.534 --> 00:10:18.033
of virtually the entire
Republican Party.

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:20.200
It's a movement fully
in thrall to Trumpism,

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.000
which is why we have
to investigate what they did

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.400
and make sure
it never happens again,

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:27.434
especially since Trump keeps
teasing another run in 2024,

00:10:27.434 --> 00:10:30.334
because there were times
when Trump was so abjectly,

00:10:30.334 --> 00:10:31.701
brazenly, criminally...
-Stupid.

00:10:31.701 --> 00:10:33.667
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:33.667 --> 00:10:37.534
♪♪

00:10:37.534 --> 00:10:38.901
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:10:38.901 --> 00:10:40.367
over two million meals a year

00:10:40.367 --> 00:10:42.534
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:10:42.534 --> 00:10:44.634
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:10:44.634 --> 00:10:46.133
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:10:46.133 --> 00:10:48.834
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:10:48.834 --> 00:10:51.467
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

